# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.

# Plan 00201 (pingbus fix and final review fixes): deploys the ccy launcher 3.98.7, which
# requires container 2.62, so the next ccy launch rebuilds the image once. The image gets the
# pingbus whose target refusals name what was refused and who can be addressed, and the member
# kit's new settings.json, whose status line is `pingbus status-line`: a team session shows
# `bus: A,B` in any checkout. Also deploys cc-teams.bash (`cc --teams` makes .claude/ccy/ only
# after the consent). Running ccy sessions keep their old image until each is relaunched.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
# Plan 00201: agent-bus-install software puts the same kit settings and pingbus in
# /usr/local/share/agent-bus/kit, which cc --teams and agent-bus-claude launch with. No team,
# homeserver or firewall rule changes.
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml
# Plan 00201: the automated two-team acceptance again, since its M3 leg now checks
# `pingbus status-line` in the session's container (the checkout's own status line, then
# `bus: A,B`). Then the owner's steps in ACCEPTANCE-owner.md, from another project's checkout.
00201-ccy-teams-many-teams-per-session-descriptions-and-a-picker

# Plan 00199: rebuilds md-viewer at the M12 commit (non-regular files never block, tracked-files-only
# label test); nothing else changes.
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-md-viewer.yml
